{title: Blessed Assurance}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}
{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Blessed as[C]surance, [F]Jesus is [C]mine!
O what a [Am]foretaste of [D]glory di[G]vine!
Heir of sal[C]vation, [F]purchase of [C]God
Born of his [Dm]Spirit, [G]washed in his [C]blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
This is my [C]story, [F]this is my [C]song
Praising my [Am]Savior [D]all the day [G]long
[G]This is my [C]story, [F]this is my [C]song
Praising my [Dm]Savior [G]all the day [C]long.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Perfect sub[C]mission, perfect de[**]light
Visions of [Am]rapture now [D]burst on my [G]sight
Angels des[C]cending [F]bring from a[C]bove
Echoes of [Dm]mercy, [G]whispers of [C]love.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Perfect sub[C]mission, [F]all is at [C]rest
I in my [Am]Savior am [D]happy and [G]blessed
Watching and [C]waiting, looking a[**]bove
Filled with his [Dm]goodness, [G]lost in his [C]love.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
